8-windsor-ruins.html", "mongo_id": null, "parent_id": 39211048, "parent_type": "Route", "created_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "updated_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "community_poi_id": null, "locality": null, "administrative_area": null, "country_code": null, "location_hex": null, "v": 0, "t": 14, "n": "Windsor Ruins", "d": "Built in 1859-61, Windsor plantation was used as a Union hospital and observation post during the Civil War. After the Civil War, during a house party on February 17, 1890 a guest left a lighted cigar on the upper balcony and Windsor burned to the ground. Everything was destroyed except 23 of the columns, balustrades and iron stairs.", "pids": [12103988, 12103986, 12103987], "uid": 4462745}, {"id": 59716993, "lng": -91.126541, "lat": 31.894384, "url": "https://www.natcheztracetravel.com/lorman-bedandbreakfasts/canemount.html", "mongo_id": null, "parent_id": 39211048, "parent_type": "Route", "created_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "updated_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "community_poi_id": null, "locality": null, "administrative_area": null, "country_code": null, "location_hex": null, "v": 0, "t": 10, "n": "Canemount Plantation Inn B&B", "d": "Canemount Plantation B&B is located in Claiborne County, MS - two miles north of Alcorn State University, three miles south of Windsor Ruins, fourteen miles south of Port Gibson, MS.", "pids": [12103488, 12103486, 12103487], "uid": 4462745}, {"id": 59716994, "lng": -91.131485, "lat": 31.883106, "url": null, "mongo_id": null, "parent_id": 39211048, "parent_type": "Route", "created_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "updated_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "community_poi_id": null, "locality": null, "administrative_area": null, "country_code": null, "location_hex": null, "v": 0, "t": 13, "n": "CJ's Place", "d": "Open Monday thru Friday for lunch and dinner. 1054 MS-552, Lorman, MS", "pids": [], "uid": 4462745}, {"id": 59716995, "lng": -91.13842, "lat": 31.87989, "url": null, "mongo_id": null, "parent_id": 39211048, "parent_type": "Route", "created_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "updated_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "community_poi_id": null, "locality": null, "administrative_area": null, "country_code": null, "location_hex": null, "v": 0, "t": 13, "n": "Patton's Store", "d": "Open 7 days a week for lunch and dinner. 5185 Highway 552, Lorman, MS", "pids": [], "uid": 4462745}, {"id": 59716996, "lng": -91.057388, "lat": 31.843786, "url": "https://www.natcheztracetravel.com/natchez-trace-mississippi/exits/486-mississippi-highway-552.html", "mongo_id": null, "parent_id": 39211048, "parent_type": "Route", "created_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "updated_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "community_poi_id": null, "locality": null, "administrative_area": null, "country_code": null, "location_hex": null, "v": 0, "t": 17, "n": "Mississippi Highway 552", "d": "Access/exit road intersection to the Parkway at milepost 30.", "pids": [], "uid": 4462745}, {"id": 59716997, "lng": -91.050797, "lat": 31.820017, "url": "https://www.natcheztracetravel.com/natchez-trace-mississippi/lorman-natchez-ms/oldcountrystore.html", "mongo_id": null, "parent_id": 39211048, "parent_type": "Route", "created_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "updated_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "community_poi_id": null, "locality": null, "administrative_area": null, "country_code": null, "location_hex": null, "v": 0, "t": 13, "n": "The Old Country Store Restaurant", "d": "People travel for hours to partake of Mr D's 'Heavenly Fried Chicken' at The Old Country Store Restaurant in Lorman, Mississippi. The restaurant is on US 61 between Port Gibson and Natchez just off the Natchez Trace Parkway. 18801 Highway 61 Lorman, MS", "pids": [], "uid": 4462745}, {"id": 59716998, "lng": -91.12918853759767, "lat": 31.906089604916776, "url": "https://www.natcheztracetravel.com/natchez-trace-mississippi/loop-routes/windsor-ruins.html", "mongo_id": null, "parent_id": 39211048, "parent_type": "Route", "created_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "updated_at": "2022-04-26T14:09:20-07:00", "community_poi_id": null, "locality": null, "administrative_area": null, "country_code": null, "location_hex": null, "v": 0, "t": 14, "n": "Bethel Church", "d": "The original congregation of the Bethel Presbyterian Church organized in 1826 under the direction of Dr. Jeremiah Chamberlain. The building, that still stands today, was built in the mid 1840s. During Grant\u2019s campaign to take Vicksburg, he landed his troops east of the Mississippi River just a few miles from here at Bruinsburg. His troops passed Bethel Church on April 30th, 1863 moving to Port Gibson on the Rodney Road.", "pids": [12208777], "uid": 4462745}]}}